From: Mikhail Zinchenko <m1d3ry@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:24:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make WalkDirectory take a forwarding reference

`WalkDirectory` declared its visitor as `Lambda&`, a non-const lvalue reference. Its call sites in
`OpenFile` and `GetFilesByLastModDate` pass a temporary lambda. A conforming compiler rejects the bind
of an rvalue to a non-const lvalue reference, so the file only compiles under the permissive mode of
MSVC. clang-cl rejects it.

`Lambda&&` is a forwarding reference. It binds the temporary at the two call sites and also the lvalue
`visitor` in the recursive call, so the behaviour under MSVC does not change.
---
 src/msix/PAL/FileSystem/Win32/DirectoryObject.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/msix/PAL/FileSystem/Win32/DirectoryObject.cpp b/src/msix/PAL/FileSystem/Win32/DirectoryObject.cpp
index 5cfcdb8e..df14e01d 100644
--- a/src/msix/PAL/FileSystem/Win32/DirectoryObject.cpp
+++ b/src/msix/PAL/FileSystem/Win32/DirectoryObject.cpp
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ namespace MSIX
         }
 
         template <class Lambda>
-        void WalkDirectory(const std::string& root, WalkOptions options, Lambda& visitor)
+        void WalkDirectory(const std::string& root, WalkOptions options, Lambda&& visitor)
         {
             static std::string dot(".");
             static std::string dotdot("..");
